This follows the standard benchmarks-game binary-trees program.

- maxDepth = max(minDepth + 2, N), with minDepth = 4. For small N, the stretch tree uses maxDepth+1 and the long-lived tree uses maxDepth. The spec's "N+1" is satisfied for N ≥ 6. For smaller N, the standard program prints maxDepth. I'll follow the standard behavior.
- Stretch tree: depth maxDepth+1, printed as `stretch tree of depth X\t check: count`.
- For each d from 4 to maxDepth in steps of 2: iterations = 2^(maxDepth-d+4). Print `iterations\t trees of depth d\t check: sum`.
- Long-lived tree: depth maxDepth.

Checksum is the node count of each tree. With depth d, the count is 2^(d+1)-1.

For speed, a node is an object with left and right fields. A tree is built recursively, then the check walks it. Garbage collection handles the "free".

For a leaf, I use `{left:null,right:null}`. The checker counts 1 + check(left) + check(right) when left is non-null.

Output uses `\t` as in the standard format: "stretch tree of depth 17\t check: 262143". The trees line is `${iter}\t trees of depth ${d}\t check: ${sum}`.

For N=0 or 1, maxDepth = 6 under the standard program, so output would be for depth 6. I'm going with the standard.

```javascript
function Node(l, r) {
  this.left = l;
  this.right = r;
}

function bottomUp(d) {
  if (d === 0) return new Node(null, null);
  return new Node(bottomUp(d - 1), bottomUp(d - 1));
}

function check(t) {
  if (t.left === null) return 1;
  return 1 + check(t.left) + check(t.right);
}

function main() {
  const n = parseInt(process.argv[2], 10) || 0;
  const minDepth = 4;
  const maxDepth = Math.max(minDepth + 2, n);
  const out = [];

  const stretch = maxDepth + 1;
  out.push("stretch tree of depth " + stretch + "\t check: " + check(bottomUp(stretch)));

  const longLived = bottomUp(maxDepth);

  for (let d = minDepth; d <= maxDepth; d += 2) {
    const iters = 1 << (maxDepth - d + minDepth);
    let sum = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < iters; i++) {
      sum += check(bottomUp(d));
    }
    out.push(iters + "\t trees of depth " + d + "\t check: " + sum);
  }

  out.push("long lived tree of depth " + maxDepth + "\t check: " + check(longLived));
  console.log(out.join("\n"));
}

main();
```

